  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 127 PM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nStrong upper ridging currently centered over the central High Plains\ncontinues to support hot conditions across the forecast area, with \nheat indices in the 105-110 range this afternoon. Ensemble and \ndeterministic guidance show the upper ridge beginning to shift west \nand south by Tuesday. A shortwave trough moving through the northern\nPlains will drive a cold front south across northeast Kansas during \nthe day. This should lead to a slightly cooler day as dewpoints fall \nthrough the afternoon behind the front. Wednesday, it will feel \nnoticeably cooler with highs in the 80s and dewpoints in the 50s. As \nthe front settles just south of the area, shortwave energy embedded \nwithin northwest flow aloft will bring increasing chances for showers\nand thunderstorms Wednesday night into Thursday. Associated cloud \ncover should also help keep highs near to below climatological \nnormal for this time of the year, with highs in the upper 70s to low \n80s. By Friday into the weekend, the upper ridge is favored to \nre\u2011expand eastward from the southern Plains, allowing a return to \nwarmer temperatures with highs back into the lower to mid\u201190s and \nlower, more isolated thunderstorm chances.",
